nt Party (USDP) emerged as a pivotal political entity in Myanmar following the controversial 2010 general elections, which marked a significant transition from decades of military rule to a quasi-democratic system. Headquartered in Dekkhinathiri Township, Naypyidaw, the party was established by the military-backed regime, primarily to facilitate a semblance of democratic governance while retaining military control over the political landscape. Key figures in its formation included former military leaders and government officials, who sought to stabilize their power amidst increasing domestic and international calls for reform.

